      "targetId": "harness-mandate-digest-invalid-hex-authority",
      "claim": "mandate.py's _digest helper validates only the sha256: prefix and total length (71 chars) for every runtime digest field (HarnessMandateConsumption.mandate_digest, HarnessExecutionProfile.tool_catalog_digest/tool_grant_digest, HarnessExecutionStrategy.mandate_digest, CompiledHarnessAttempt mandate/profile/strategy digests), but never validates that the 64-character hex payload only contains [0-9a-f]. This is inconsistent with core_contracts._digest which enforces the strict _DIGEST_RE ^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$. As a result, a structurally invalid digest such as 'sha256:' + 'g'*64 is admitted into consumption/recipient authority evidence, violating the sha256 hex canonical form contract.",
